## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical AWS multi-tenant isolation at scale, combining IAM session tags, Lake Formation, data catalog usage, and automated revocation; probes policy design, GitOps deployment, and testing.

## Key Concepts
- IAM role session tags
- Lake Formation permissions
- Data catalog integration
- Event-driven revocation with DynamoDB, EventBridge, Step Functions
- GitOps deployment of IAM policies
- Auditability: CloudTrail, Config, Access Analyzer

## Code Example
```json
// Trust policy snippet (AssumeRole requires matching tenant-id tag)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      },
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/PrincipalRoleForTenant"}
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// Permission policy snippet (tenant-scoped S3 and Lake Formation actions)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-data/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*",
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-data/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["lakeformation:GetDataAccess"],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"lakeformation:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test cross-tenant leakage with automated CI checks?
- What monitoring would you add to detect revocation failures and alert on latency breaches?

